  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "%lld complete" : {
      "comment" : "Part of a compact one-line summary under each finished archive, which the app joins as '12 complete · 1 partial · 0 not saved'. %lld is the number of files that were extracted in full and passed their integrity checks. 'Complete' describes the files (an adjective, as in 'complete files'); it is not an instruction. Keep it very short. You may reorder the number and the word, or use a form like 'Complete: %lld', if your grammar needs it.",
