    "Bring your classic Mac archives back." : {
      "comment" : "Tagline under the app's name at the top of the main window. Warm and brief: the app lets people open decades-old compressed files from their old Macintosh again. 'Bring back' means make usable again, with a hint of nostalgia; it does not mean returning goods. Keep 'Mac' as written. 'Classic' refers to the classic Mac OS era - Macintosh computers of the 1980s and 1990s - not 'classical' or 'traditional'. 'Archive' means a compressed file container (like a .zip file) - here an old StuffIt .sit file - not a records archive, an archive room, or a backup.",
