    "Classic .sit archives" : {
      "comment" : "Small caption in the drop area telling the user which kind of file is accepted. '.sit' is a file name extension; keep it exactly as written, including the dot. 'Classic' refers to the classic Mac OS era - Macintosh computers of the 1980s and 1990s - not 'classical' or 'traditional'. 'Archive' means a compressed file container (like a .zip file) - here an old StuffIt .sit file - not a records archive, an archive room, or a backup.",
